Started adding the YAML validation, but turns out QuartoDoc is a bit more complicated then my test case so I'm getting some confusing behavior.  What I recommend is that we pair program on some of the most hairy bits together.  

~One test fails on purpose - might be best if we pair on this @machow when you are back.   One error that is confusing for example is when I leave the `name` field out under `contents`, like this:~ EDIT I made those pass 😆 

@machow lets sync when you are back.  I made it kind of far but the key is adding lots and lots of tests I think

This attempts to addresses https://github.com/machow/quartodoc/issues/223 by adding files we might want to ignore

I wasn't able to repro https://github.com/machow/quartodoc/issues/223 but I made a best effort based on the comments around ignoring `__pycache__` which seems reasonable.  I also added similar directories we wanted to ignore.  

@machow @wch do you want to test this branch to see if it solves the issue?
